    "recommendation": "Verify the control evaluation and any approved exception; restore the intended control through change management, revoke suspicious sessions, and review authentication methods and policy changes. For “Conditional Access Policy Bypass Attempt”, verify the exact policy/control outcome and any approved exception or configuration change.",
    "analysisGuide": {
      "logsTelemetry": "SigninLogs; Conditional Access evaluation details; authentication-method and directory audit logs; identity protection/risk events; device compliance and client-app telemetry.",
      "investigationPivots": "Compare policy result, applied policies, exclusions, client app, authentication strength, MFA claim, device compliance and policy change history. Correlate the sign-in with recent changes to authentication methods or policy scope.",
      "redFlags": "Unexpected policy exclusion; successful access despite expected control; legacy client; MFA method added shortly before sign-in; unmanaged/noncompliant device; repeated prompts or unexpected interrupted/success transitions. Alert-specific focus: Conditional Access Policy Bypass Attempt. Validate this behavior using raw telemetry and related events; the alert title alone is not proof.",
      "precautionPrevention": "Use least-privilege policy exclusions, require strong MFA and compliant devices for sensitive apps, block legacy authentication, review policy changes and test policies in report-only/staged mode before enforcement.",
      "ifCompromise": "Verify the control evaluation and any approved exception; restore the intended control through change management, revoke suspicious sessions, and review authentication methods and policy changes.",
      "evidenceToCollect": "Sign-in ID/time; user and app; Conditional Access policy IDs/results; client app; MFA/authentication details; device ID/compliance; policy change audit event; source IP; request/correlation ID; approved exception/change ticket."
    }
