    "recommendation": "Review app publisher, permissions and consent actor; revoke unauthorized grants and assess API/mail/file access performed by the app. For “Unusual Application Sign-In”, inspect the exact application identity, granted scopes and any subsequent API/resource access.",
    "analysisGuide": {
      "logsTelemetry": "Entra ID AuditLogs and service principal sign-in logs; OAuth consent/grant events; application permissions and service-principal inventory; mailbox/file activity where relevant.",
      "investigationPivots": "Identify app/client ID, publisher/owner, requested permissions, consenting user, grant type, redirect URI and creation time. Compare permissions with app purpose and check subsequent API, mailbox, SharePoint or cloud activity.",
      "redFlags": "Unverified publisher; broad mail/files/directory permissions; consent from privileged user; unfamiliar redirect URI; app created shortly before consent; suspicious API activity or persistence after consent. Alert-specific focus: Unusual Application Sign-In. Validate this behavior using raw telemetry and related events; the alert title alone is not proof.",
      "precautionPrevention": "Restrict user consent, use admin consent workflow, review high-privilege grants and enterprise apps, require verified publishers where possible, and periodically remove unused grants.",
      "ifCompromise": "Review app publisher, permissions and consent actor; revoke unauthorized grants and assess API/mail/file access performed by the app.",
      "evidenceToCollect": "App/client and service-principal IDs; publisher; permissions/scopes; consenting identity; grant type; redirect URI; timestamp; audit event IDs; sign-in/API activity; affected resources; revocation and owner-confirmation records."
    }
