    "recommendation": "Validate the identity event with the account owner and authentication telemetry; protect the account and revoke sessions if unauthorized activity is supported. For “Disabled Account Sign-In Attempt”, explicitly compare the relevant account/source pattern and the successful/failed authentication sequence.",
    "analysisGuide": {
      "logsTelemetry": "Entra ID SigninLogs / non-interactive sign-in logs; identity provider authentication events; MFA and Conditional Access results; VPN, proxy and source-IP telemetry; Windows Security events where applicable.",
      "investigationPivots": "Pivot from user and source IP to 30–60 minutes before/after the event. Compare failed and successful attempts, app/resource, device ID, user agent, ASN/location, MFA result and session/token activity. Check other accounts from the same IP and other IPs used by the same account.",
      "redFlags": "Many failures followed by success; one source targeting many users; new ASN/device/user agent; unfamiliar country or hosting provider; MFA absent or repeatedly denied; successful sign-in followed by mailbox, privilege or token changes. Alert-specific focus: Disabled Account Sign-In Attempt. Validate this behavior using raw telemetry and related events; the alert title alone is not proof.",
      "precautionPrevention": "Require phishing-resistant MFA where feasible; block legacy auth; review Conditional Access and risk policies; protect privileged accounts; alert on spray patterns and monitor sign-in baselines.",
      "ifCompromise": "Validate the identity event with the account owner and authentication telemetry; protect the account and revoke sessions if unauthorized activity is supported.",
      "evidenceToCollect": "UTC timestamps; user/object ID; source IP/ASN/location; application/resource; status/error code; correlation/request IDs; device/user agent; MFA and Conditional Access details; related event IDs; user/owner validation; response actions."
    }
